# Node modules, at any depth. Was scoped to extensions/ for the Tailwind
# builds, which left the client packages under packages/ and an npm install at
# the repo root showing up in every `git status` and one careless `git add .`
# away from being committed. A bare directory pattern matches at every level,
# so it covers all three.
node_modules/

# Worktrees
.worktrees/

# Compiled example/demo binaries. Go names the output after its directory, so
# these have no extension and are easy to sweep in with `git add -A` after a
# build. Each is 50-90 MB.
examples/*/[!.]*
!examples/*/*.*
!examples/*/*/
extensions/*/examples/*/[!.]*
!extensions/*/examples/*/*.*
!extensions/*/examples/*/*/

# Compiled cmd/ binaries dropped at the repo root. `go build ./cmd/<name>` run
# from here writes the output beside go.mod, named after the directory and with
# no extension -- the same trap as the example binaries above, and the same
# 30-90 MB. Listed by name rather than matched by a root-level pattern, because
# Dockerfile, LICENSE, Makefile and TRADEMARKS are extensionless files at the
# root that must stay tracked. Add a line here when a new cmd/ package lands.
/dashboard-contract-probe
/forge

# Claude Code working directories. .claude/worktrees holds full checkouts of
# this repository -- 580 MB at the time of writing -- so a `git add -A` here
# commits a nested copy of the tree.
.claude/

# Superpowers scratch. These are an agent workflow's own bookkeeping -- the
# plan it is working from, the per-chunk reports it writes as it goes, the
# ledger it recovers from after a context loss. They describe how a change was
# produced rather than what the change is, so they age into a parallel and
# steadily wronger account of the codebase: a plan is a statement of intent at
# one moment, and nothing updates it when the code moves on.
#
# What such a document is genuinely for belongs somewhere durable instead -- a
# design decision in the code comment beside the decision, an ADR, a commit
# message, a docs/ page that is maintained. What is left is process exhaust,
# and the repository is not its home.
#
# `.superpowers/` is the live workspace and self-ignores via its own .gitignore;
# it is named here anyway so the rule does not depend on a file the tooling
# happens to write.
.superpowers/
.superpowers-report-*.md
docs/superpowers/
